From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: prospero-win <prospero-win@invalid>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 17:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Read and write this process without the server.

NtWriteVirtualMemory always asks the server to write, and the server
reaches a process with process_vm_writev or ptrace. A PS5 title has
neither, so every WriteProcessMemory a program made to itself failed:
Project Reclaimer's engine worker could not hand Halo 3 its asset paths,
key bindings or controller settings, and kept retrying every frame.
NtReadVirtualMemory already copies in process for the pseudo-handle, but
a real handle to this process (OpenProcess( GetCurrentProcessId() ), as
toolhelp's module snapshot uses) still went to the server and failed the
same way, so Module32First found no modules.

Treat any handle that names this process as the current process: reads
keep their guarded copy, and writes use virtual_uninterrupted_write_memory,
which checks each page's access without faulting and keeps write watches
current. WriteProcessMemory has already made read-only pages writable, as
on Windows. Other processes still go through the server.
---
 dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c | 35 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 33 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
@@ -6816,6 +6816,23 @@
 
 
 /***********************************************************************
+ *           is_this_process
+ *
+ * Whether a process handle names this process: the pseudo-handle, or a
+ * real handle such as OpenProcess( GetCurrentProcessId() ) returns.
+ */
+static BOOL is_this_process( HANDLE process )
+{
+    PROCESS_BASIC_INFORMATION pbi;
+
+    if (process == GetCurrentProcess()) return TRUE;
+    if (NtQueryInformationProcess( process, ProcessBasicInformation, &pbi, sizeof(pbi), NULL ))
+        return FALSE;
+    return pbi.UniqueProcessId == HandleToULong( NtCurrentTeb()->ClientId.UniqueProcess );
+}
+
+
+/***********************************************************************
  *             NtReadVirtualMemory   (NTDLL.@)
  *             ZwReadVirtualMemory   (NTDLL.@)
  */
@@ -6829,7 +6846,7 @@
         status = STATUS_ACCESS_VIOLATION;
         size = 0;
     }
-    else if (process == GetCurrentProcess())
+    else if (is_this_process( process ))
     {
         __TRY
         {
@@ -6868,7 +6885,21 @@
 {
     unsigned int status;
 
-    if (virtual_check_buffer_for_read( buffer, size ))
+    if (virtual_check_buffer_for_read( buffer, size ) && is_this_process( process ))
+    {
+        /* Write into this process here rather than through the server,
+         * which needs process_vm_writev or ptrace to reach a process. A
+         * PS5 title has neither, so every WriteProcessMemory to itself
+         * failed there. WriteProcessMemory has already made read-only
+         * pages writable; this checks access per page, without faulting,
+         * and keeps write watches up to date. */
+        if ((status = virtual_uninterrupted_write_memory( addr, buffer, size )))
+        {
+            status = STATUS_PARTIAL_COPY;
+            size = 0;
+        }
+    }
+    else if (virtual_check_buffer_for_read( buffer, size ))
     {
         SERVER_START_REQ( write_process_memory )
         {
-- 
